      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 49-year-old man developed a syndrome of crural-axial dystonia combined with segmental myoclonus 3 months after the onset of meralgia paraesthetica of the left leg. The association of this remarkable movement disorder with the pain syndrome is discussed."},
